commit d83ab0645b83d5f279c628e35eae0df49a92594f
Author:     ZCode <zcode@local>
AuthorDate: Sun Nov 15 17:02:03 2026 -0800
Commit:     ZCode <zcode@local>
CommitDate: Sun Nov 15 17:02:03 2026 -0800

    tests(papersim): fix CI shared-cluster isolation in native snapshot count
    
    Native run 43779672724 (0ca71e42) failed the papersim partition:
    test_native_register_verify_and_no_overwrite asserted an absolute
    'SELECT count(*) FROM papersim.snapshots' == 1, but the partition's
    nine files share one disposable managed cluster, so files that ran
    earlier (store_native/migrations/cli, including the CLI evaluate and
    replay native tests) had already registered snapshots (7 rows).
    The FX-12 node verified against an exclusive cluster, so all 51
    passed there; the environment difference exposed the isolation flaw.
    
    Count only the digest this test registers (WHERE content_sha256 = %s)
    == 1: idempotency and no-overwrite are proven per digest, independent
    of unrelated rows from earlier files. test_papersim_replay.py was
    audited in full for the same class: its native assertions are all
    digest-scoped, key-scoped (distinct scan_key/candidate_key from every
    other partition file) or before/after deltas (table_counts), so no
    change was needed. No product source touched.
    
    Evidence: full nine-file partition on one fresh throwaway shared
    cluster (09S assembly, CI order): 280 passed; focused verbose trio
    (cli -> snapshots -> replay, same shared DB, 4 unrelated snapshot
    rows present): 85 passed with the previously failing test named
    PASSED; verify_local.py --full in a cleaned env on Linux: 41826
    passed, 154 skipped; compile/diff-check clean; papersim selfcheck
    byte-identical before/after (a4aa971f, 1663B).

