src/polymarket_alpha_lab/replay.py
1: """FX-12 candidate binding and forensic replay of paper decisions.
2: 
3: Two faces of one contract (M1 plan section 3 FX-12, items 2 and 3):
4: 
5: RECORD SIDE -- binding. :func:`bind_candidate` turns one
6: :class:`~polymarket_alpha_lab.papersim.pipeline.EntryRequest` plus its
7: :class:`~polymarket_alpha_lab.papersim.pipeline.EntryDecision` into a
8: :class:`~polymarket_alpha_lab.papersim.store.CandidateSubmission` whose
9: ``input_payload`` is a canonical, version-pinned replay bundle carrying
10: the decision-time evidence -- the raw model quote (xG/soccer or the
11: original crypto probability record), the RAW order-book ladder, the
12: league-strength kappa ``bridge`` table, the news record, the portfolio
13: state (bankroll/cash/reserved/held sides/team exposure), the decision
14: clock (``book_time``/``now``/``max_book_age_seconds``), and the fee and
15: configuration evidence. ``snapshot_refs`` cite raw evidence bytes
16: registered through :mod:`polymarket_alpha_lab.papersim.snapshots`, the
17: gate report JSON carries the full ordered reason record, and the code
18: commit rides on the scan run row. Rejected AND construction-failed
19: candidates bind the same way (:func:`bind_construction_failure`
20: re-runs the pure constructor so the recorded failure is the observed
21: one).
22: 
23: REPLAY SIDE -- forensics. :func:`replay` is READ-ONLY取证 over a
24: supplied managed connection: it re-reads the candidate, its scan run,
25: its decision-time price evidence and every cited snapshot; verifies
26: each snapshot's hash, byte length and (optionally) schema version
27: against the stored bytes; refuses to run unless the recorded code
28: commit equals the operator-supplied TRUSTED commit (the current HEAD
29: never silently substitutes for the recorded one) and the recomputed
30: policy fingerprint matches the recorded one; then recomputes
31: :func:`~polymarket_alpha_lab.papersim.pipeline.decide_entry` in the
32: reviewed fixed environment and compares EVERY field -- conclusion,
33: ordered reasons, per-step statuses, sizing, fees, walks, bridge
34: fingerprint and version pins -- under one rounding policy. Nothing is
35: fetched from the network, no code from the record is executed (only
36: the reviewed library's own pure functions run), missing evidence or a
37: missing snapshot is an explicit failure, and the module issues SELECT
38: statements only: replay never writes a row, never adds an entry and
39: never opens a connection itself.
40: 
41: Paper boundary: binding and replay are paper-evidence operations only
42: (``paper_only``/``report_only``/``readonly``); they grant no execution
43: authorization and never touch an order.
44: """
45: 
46: from __future__ import annotations
47: 
